For large collections, use virtualized rendering, such as `react-virtual`, to avoid rendering hundreds or thousands of cards simultaneously.

## 3.5 Farm card structure

Each card contains:

| Element | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Status dot | Quick visual condition indicator |
| Thumbnail | Satellite preview of the farm |
| Farm name | Farm identification |
| Area | Total registered geographic area |
| Crop | Current recorded crop, if known |
| Status badge | Current condition classification |
| Chevron | Indicates selection/navigation |

Example:

```tsx
interface FarmCardProps {
  farm: Farm;
  selected: boolean;
  onClick: () => void;
}
```

Example rendering:

```tsx
function FarmCard({
  farm,
  selected,
  onClick
}: FarmCardProps) {

  return (
    <button
      className={`farm-card ${selected ? "selected" : ""}`}
      onClick={onClick}
    >

      <div className="farm-thumbnail">

        <img
          src={farm.thumbnailUrl}
          alt=""
        />

        <FarmStatusDot
          status={farm.healthStatus}
        />

      </div>

      <div className="farm-card-content">

        <h3>{farm.name}</h3>

        <p>
          {formatArea(farm.areaHa)}
          {" • "}
          {farm.currentCrop ?? "Crop not recorded"}
        </p>

        <FarmStatusBadge
          status={farm.healthStatus}
        />

      </div>

      <ChevronRight />

    </button>
  );
}
```

The card must be clickable across its entire surface.

The thumbnail is not an independently stored illustration if it can be generated from the actual farm geometry and satellite basemap.

A practical thumbnail generation strategy is:

1. Load the farm polygon.
2. Calculate its geographic bounding box.
3. Expand the bounds slightly.
4. Request a static satellite map image.
5. Draw the polygon outline over the image.
6. Crop to the farm aspect ratio.
7. Cache the result.

If a thumbnail cannot be generated, display a neutral fallback image rather than a broken image icon.

