# 7. GLOBAL GEOGRAPHIC SEARCH

The map contains a search bar near its upper-left corner.

Visible placeholder:

`Search anywhere in the world...`

This search is independent of the farm search.

It should allow users to search for:

- Countries.
- Cities.
- Towns.
- Villages.
- Addresses.
- Regions.
- Geographic coordinates.
- Known landmarks.

## 7.1 Search component

```tsx
function MapSearch() {

  const [query, setQuery] = useState("");

  const [results, setResults] = useState([]);

  async function searchLocation(value: string) {

    setQuery(value);

    if (value.trim().length < 2) {
      setResults([]);
      return;
    }

    const data = await geocodingApi.search(value);

    setResults(data);
  }

  return (
    <div className="map-search">

      <SearchIcon />

      <input
        value={query}
        onChange={e => searchLocation(e.target.value)}
        placeholder="Search anywhere in the world..."
      />

      <SearchResults results={results} />

    </div>
  );
}
```

Use debouncing so that every keystroke does not trigger a network request.

```ts
const DEBOUNCE_MS = 350;
```

Additional search requirements:

- Cancel obsolete requests when a new query is submitted.
- Display loading feedback.
- Display a useful no-results state.
- Distinguish ambiguous places.
- Support keyboard navigation.
- Respect geocoding provider rate limits.

## 7.2 Search result selection

When the user selects a location:

```ts
function navigateToLocation(result: GeocodingResult) {

  map.flyTo({
    center: [
      result.longitude,
      result.latitude
    ],

    zoom: result.suggestedZoom ?? 13,

    duration: 1400
  });
}
```

The zoom should depend on the result type.

Example policy:

| Result type | Suggested zoom |
|---|---:|
| Country | 4 |
| Large region | 7 |
| City | 11 |
| Town | 13 |
| Street/address | 16 |
| Exact coordinate | 16 |

These are initial configuration values, not fixed geographic laws.

If a location is outside the currently visible area, the map must navigate smoothly to it.

