# 8. LOCATE-ME CONTROL

The circular crosshair control beside the search field requests the user's current geographic location.

```tsx
<button
  aria-label="Locate my position"
  onClick={locateUser}
>
  <CrosshairIcon />
</button>
```

Implementation:

```ts
async function locateUser() {

  if (!navigator.geolocation) {
    showError("Location is not supported.");
    return;
  }

  navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition(
    position => {

      const longitude =
        position.coords.longitude;

      const latitude =
        position.coords.latitude;

      map.flyTo({
        center: [longitude, latitude],
        zoom: 15,
        duration: 1200
      });

    },

    error => {
      showLocationError(error);
    },

    {
      enableHighAccuracy: true,
      timeout: 10000,
      maximumAge: 30000
    }
  );
}
```

Requirements:

- Ask for browser permission.
- Never assume permission has been granted.
- Handle permission denial.
- Handle unavailable location.
- Handle timeout.
- Do not continuously track users unless they explicitly activate a tracking feature.
- Do not persist precise location unnecessarily.

