# 9. FARM BOUNDARY VISUALIZATION

The map shows farm boundaries as polygon overlays.

Each polygon represents the actual geographic geometry stored for a farm.

The screenshot demonstrates three different boundary states:

- Green polygon: Healthy.
- Amber polygon: Moderate.
- Red polygon: At Risk.

The selected farm is visually distinguished from unselected farms.

## 9.1 GeoJSON feature structure

Each farm should be converted into a map feature.

```ts
interface FarmMapFeature {
  type: "Feature";

  id: string;

  geometry: GeoJSON.Polygon |
            GeoJSON.MultiPolygon;

  properties: {
    farmId: string;
    farmName: string;

    healthStatus: FarmHealthStatus;

    areaHa: number;

    selected: boolean;
  };
}
```

Example:

```json
{
  "type": "Feature",
  "id": "farm-001",
  "geometry": {
    "type": "Polygon",
    "coordinates": [
      [
        [55.1000, 25.1000],
        [55.1050, 25.1000],
        [55.1070, 25.1050],
        [55.1010, 25.1070],
        [55.1000, 25.1000]
      ]
    ]
  },
  "properties": {
    "farmId": "farm-001",
    "farmName": "Green Valley Farm",
    "healthStatus": "healthy",
    "areaHa": 78.3,
    "selected": true
  }
}
```

## 9.2 Polygon fill

Use a translucent fill so the underlying satellite imagery remains visible.

Example:

```ts
const fillColors = {
  healthy: "#31D96B",
  moderate: "#FFB21A",
  at_risk: "#F04452",
  no_data: "#929CA6"
};
```

Example Mapbox layer:

```ts
map.addLayer({
  id: "farm-fill",

  type: "fill",

  source: "farms",

  paint: {

    "fill-color": [
      "match",

      ["get", "healthStatus"],

      "healthy", "#31D96B",

      "moderate", "#FFB21A",

      "at_risk", "#F04452",

      "#929CA6"
    ],

    "fill-opacity": 0.30
  }
});
```

## 9.3 Polygon outline

```ts
map.addLayer({
  id: "farm-outline",

  type: "line",

  source: "farms",

  paint: {

    "line-color": [
