# 10. FARM AREA LABELS

The screenshot displays area labels inside each polygon.

Examples:

```text
78.3 ha
120.1 ha
64.2 ha
```

These labels should be generated from actual farm area data.

Do not manually position labels using fixed screen coordinates.

## 10.1 Label position

A simple polygon centroid may fall outside a concave polygon.

Use a point-on-surface or pole-of-inaccessibility algorithm to find a label position that lies inside the polygon.

Possible tools:

- Turf.js `pointOnFeature`.
- Turf.js `centerOfMass` with containment verification.
- A polylabel implementation.

Example:

```ts
const labelPoint = polylabel(
  polygonCoordinates,
  precision
);
```

The label should update when:

- The polygon changes.
- The map feature is reloaded.
- The geometry is edited.
- The selected map data changes.

## 10.2 Label display

```tsx
<div className="farm-area-label">
  {farm.areaHa.toFixed(1)} ha
</div>
```

The map renderer should preferably use symbol layers or geographic markers rather than ordinary HTML elements fixed to the screen.

The label must remain geographically attached to its farm while panning and zooming.

At low zoom levels, hide or cluster labels if they become too dense.

