# 12. MAP NAVIGATION CONTROLS

The right edge of the screenshot contains a vertical control stack.

It has four controls:

1. Locate or orientation/navigation control.
2. Zoom in.
3. Zoom out.
4. Map layers.
5. Fullscreen.

The screenshot visually groups some controls together, but each must have its own clearly defined function.

## 12.1 Zoom in

```ts
function zoomIn() {
  map.zoomTo(
    map.getZoom() + 1,
    { duration: 250 }
  );
}
```

## 12.2 Zoom out

```ts
function zoomOut() {
  map.zoomTo(
    map.getZoom() - 1,
    { duration: 250 }
  );
}
```

Respect the map's minimum and maximum zoom levels.

## 12.3 Orientation/reset bearing

The navigation control should return the map to a north-up orientation.

```ts
function resetBearing() {

  map.easeTo({
    bearing: 0,
    pitch: 0,
    duration: 500
  });

}
```

If the first icon is intended to locate the user, use the browser geolocation flow described earlier instead. Do not combine two unrelated actions in one ambiguous control.

## 12.4 Map layer selector

The layers button opens a compact map-style menu.

Potential options:

- Satellite.
- Satellite with labels.
- Streets.
- Terrain.
- Hybrid.

These are basemap styles, not agricultural analysis layers.

```ts
type BasemapStyle =
  | "satellite"
  | "satellite-streets"
  | "streets"
  | "terrain";
