# 19. GEOMETRY VALIDATION

Before saving a farm boundary, validate it.

Checks should include:

1. Geometry type is supported.
2. Coordinates are valid numbers.
3. Longitude is between -180 and 180.
4. Latitude is between -90 and 90.
5. Polygon rings contain at least four coordinate entries, including closure.
6. At least three distinct vertices exist.
7. Polygon is closed.
8. Polygon does not self-intersect.
9. Polygon area is greater than zero.
10. Geometry is not unexpectedly enormous.
11. Holes are contained inside their outer rings.
12. Geometry is valid according to PostGIS.

Example:

```ts
function validateFarmGeometry(geometry) {

  if (!geometry) {
    throw new Error("Missing geometry");
  }

  if (!["Polygon", "MultiPolygon"].includes(
    geometry.type
  )) {
    throw new Error("Unsupported geometry type");
  }

  if (!isValidCoordinateStructure(geometry)) {
    throw new Error("Invalid coordinates");
  }

  if (!isPolygonClosed(geometry)) {
    throw new Error("Boundary is not closed");
  }

  if (hasSelfIntersections(geometry)) {
    throw new Error("Boundary intersects itself");
  }

  if (calculateAreaHa(geometry) <= 0) {
    throw new Error("Invalid farm area");
  }

  return geometry;
}
```

Use robust geometry libraries for these checks. Simple hand-written segment intersection tests are not sufficient for every geographic edge case.

The server must validate independently.

