# 24. SECURITY AND DATA OWNERSHIP

Every farm operation must be authorized on the backend.

The backend must check:

```ts
farm.userId === authenticatedUser.id
```

for all private farm read, edit and delete operations.

Never rely on hiding another user's farm in the frontend.

Additional protections:

- Validate uploaded spatial files.
- Limit upload sizes.
- Restrict geometry complexity.
- Validate all API input.
- Rate-limit geocoding requests.
- Protect API credentials.
- Log boundary changes.
- Prevent unauthorized farm ID enumeration.
- Apply database ownership checks.
- Use transactions when saving geometry and calculated metadata.

